QMX lid tray r2: the fit, the face room and the retention, from v2/cad/lid_tray_qmx_r2.py and frame_seat.out (M3 nominal +19.92, worst +16.39 for a tray 28.00 from the ceiling).
Prototype design: nothing made, printed or fitted. SCALED and INFERRED inputs are marked; the makers' figures are named.

A. JACKS AND PLUGS (tray open across both end panels above the sill; sill and keeper top 1.5 above the unit's bottom face)
   jack    panel  v from knob edge  height (scaled)   admitted plug body   who and what
   DC      L       10.2 ..  11.2      11.4 ..  12.4     d  18.8 (r  9.4)    lid harness: 12.0 V lead to A22 J_HF (2.1 x 5.5 barrel)
   Audio   L       20.4 ..  21.4       8.0 ..   9.0     d  12.0 (r  6.0)    operator: earphones (3.5 mm stereo), lid open only
   Paddle  L       32.3 ..  33.3       8.0 ..   9.0     d  12.0 (r  6.0)    operator: paddle, microphone or GPS (3.5 mm stereo), lid open only
   RF      R        7.8 ..  12.6      10.0 ..  12.1     d  16.0 (r  8.0)    lid harness: RG-316 BNC-to-SMA jumper to A22 J_RF2
   PTT     R       28.5 ..  30.2       7.4 ..   9.0     d  10.8 (r  5.4)    operator: PTT output to an amplifier (3.5 mm), lid open only
   USB     R       40.6 ..  41.6       6.3 ..   7.5     d   8.6 (r  4.3)    lid harness: USB-C lead to B16 J_QMX
   USB-C: the admitted envelope is a height, 4.3 above and below the axis; an overmold 12.35 wide (a class, INFERRED) is the other
   bound, and the unit's own panel sets it against the PTT plug: PTT to USB centres 11.4 .. 12.1 apart, so a PTT plug beside a 12.35
   overmold may be 10.5 across at most (the unit's panel, not the tray). Nothing of the tray lies within an end panel's outline above
   the sill; each end's lintel lies above the unit's top face (27.1 to 29.1 above the plate) and 3.0 wide beyond the end face, over
   every plug body; beyond the end faces only the sill or keeper (top 3.6 above the plate) and the lid plate lie under the plugs.
   Leads (permanent: DC, RF, USB; the operator's Paddle, Audio and PTT plugs come out before the lid closes, the case closes sealed):
   right panel to the flat ceiling's edge (case Y 115.93): 58.43; the RF jumper turns at R 12.5 (RG-316, the tree's figure), so its
     BNC plug may reach 42.9 from the panel before its cable turns; the USB-C lead, turning at R 20.0, 35.4.
   left panel to the flat ceiling's edge (case Y -115.93): 78.43; the DC lead loops back toward the hinge at R 20.0 west of the tray,
     so its plug may reach 55.4 from the panel. R 20.0 is the requirement on the DC and USB lead picks (not picked).

B. FACE ROOM with the lid closed (frame_seat.out M3's room between the face top and the lid ceiling: 47.92 nominal, 44.39 at the worst,
   42.11 at the worst with every unstated allowance taken twice, the case margins' sensitivity reading that decides MET)
   r2 stack from the ceiling: bond 0.20 + lid plate 2.0 + floor 1.6 + pad gap 0.5 + unit 25.0 = 29.30 to the unit's top face; + ledge 2.0 = 31.30
   (the r1 tray's 28.0 counted no lid plate; its ASSEMBLY.md row names a 2 mm nut plate the M3 row left out)
   key    min   nominal   worst  unstated x2
   M3r2a  1.00   +16.62   +13.09   +10.81  under the walls and ledges (the flat face, the light guides 0.2 proud): MET
   M3r2b  1.00   +18.62   +15.09   +12.81  under the unit's top face, over SW_MAIN, SW_PI, SW_TEST (cap heights TBD, C&K): OPEN on the cap heights (MET for caps up to 11.81, 14.09 at the worst)
   M3r2k  1.00    +7.02    +3.49    +1.21  the knob tips over the flat face (knob 11.6 above the top face, INFERRED): MET on the INFERRED knob; OPEN on its unstated height: MET for a knob up to 11.81 (14.09 at the plain worst)
   M19 (east edge at X 171.0 inside the flat ceiling): unchanged, nominal +2.08, worst +1.70, MET
   place: X 83.4 .. 171.0 (grown 18.6 west of r1's 102.0 for the gussets; the lid ceiling is free there), Y -45.8 .. 65.8
   knobs at case (X 109.4, Y -16.1) and (X 109.4, Y 36.1), each d 18.0: west of the buttons' column (X 140.4 .. 159.6) and of the light guides (X 126.4)

C. PADS (Rogers PORON 4701-30 Very Soft, 320 kg/m3, 3.18 mm (0.125 in), black (04); standing on the plate in two floor windows 24 x 20, 960 mm2)
   compression: nominal 1.08 (34 %), least 0.36 (13 %, thin pad, unit high), most 1.80 (51 %, thick pad, unit low)
   so the unit always stands on the pads, pressed up against the ledges; at 25 % the sheet gives 21 to 55 kPa, 20 to 53 N
   (the sheet states 25 % only: the preload at the least and most compression is not stated). Floor top 1.6: the hard stop toward the lid.

D. RETENTION. Unit and mated plugs 0.240 kg (maker's 220 g + 20 g INFERRED): 2.35 N per g. With the tray, keeper and plate 0.342 kg.
   Material: Prusament PC Blend (TDS v1.1): interlayer 19, flexural 87, tensile 62 MPa taken (typical less spread); printed
   floor down, 100 percent infill, 0.20 mm layers as the sheet's specimens; walls and gussets vertical, so wall tension crosses the layers.
   dir  link                                                                                                                    N        g
   out  back ledge, root bending (93.0 long, lever 2.65)                                                                     4071     1730  half the load on each side
   out  back wall, tension and bending across the layers at its root (4.3 pitches)                                           5264     2237  half the load on each wall
   out  knob-edge ledge, root bending (33.0 long, lever 2.15)                                                                1780      756  half the load on each side
   out  knob-edge wall, tension and bending across the layers at its root (4.3 pitches)                                      5607     2382  half the load on each wall
   out  M3 threads in the 2.0 lid plate, four boss screws (engagement 1.4, tip 0.6 short of the bond)                        3958     1682  INFERRED shear
   out  countersunk heads pulling through the 3.6 bosses, four                                                               6544     2781  
   out* the lid plate's DP8005 bond on the lid's polypropylene: SCOPING ONLY (T-peel of 0.5 mm HDPE x perimeter 388)          612      182  no held figure bounds it
   x    bearing of the left or right panel's bottom band on the sill or keeper (1.1 x 61 at the loose corner)                4160     1768  
   x    three M3 through the keeper and deck (or the end block), bearing on the printed holes over 3.6                       2009      854  friction not counted
   y    one wall pushed outward, bending across the layers at its root (resultant 13.0 above it, 4.3 pitches)                1655      703  lintels not counted
   Governing link on the makers' typical figures: 703 g (direction y: one wall pushed outward, bending across the layers at its root). The bond is not bounded by any held figure: its
   T-peel scoping number (182 g) is for a flexible strip, not a rigid 2 mm plate, and is no bound; it goes to CASE-MARGINS T8 as a
   pull test on the case's polypropylene.
   E1's peak on the lid is not stated by MIL-STD-810H (it sets the drop, not a pulse). Half-sine from 1.22 m over a stopping distance s:
   s  2.0 mm:  958 g;  s  5.0 mm:  383 g;  s 10.0 mm:  192 g;  s 20.0 mm:   96 g
   The known links hold to 703 g, which the bound passes for s >= 2.7 mm and fails below: a bound that includes failure. No board,
   interface or purchase depends on it (the remedy, a machined 6061 tray from the same STEP or a larger bonded plate, moves no board),
   so the retention verdict stays OPEN, allocated to E1 with an accelerometer on the lid and to T8 for the bond. E2 (MIL-STD-810H
   514.8, composite wheeled vehicle): its levels are not held here; the pads' preload and E2's 'no loosened fastener' line are the check.
   The r1 tray it replaces held the unit by one hook-and-loop strap (no figure stated) and a 6 mm lip, in PETG (HDT 68 C).

